<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Finding exponents using logarithms</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Use logarithms to find the exponent \(x\) in each equation.</p>
<p><strong>(a)</strong> \({@a@}^x = {@b@}\)</p>
<p>\(x =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p>
<div>[[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> \({@a@}^x = {@b2@}\). Give \(x\) to 2 decimal places.</p>
<p>\(x =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p>
<div>[[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>
<p>Take logarithms of both sides and use the power law \(\log(a^x) = x\log a\):</p>
\[ a^x = b \quad\Longrightarrow\quad x\log a = \log b \quad\Longrightarrow\quad x = \frac{\log b}{\log a}. \]
<p><strong>(a)</strong> \(x = \dfrac{\log {@b@}}{\log {@a@}} = {@n@}\). Check: \({@a@}^{@n@} = {@b@}\).</p>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> \(x = \dfrac{\log {@b2@}}{\log {@a@}} = {@float(ex2)@}\ldots \approx {@ta2@}\).</p>
<p>The answer lies between \({@m@}\) and \({@m+1@}\), because \({@a@}^{@m@} = {@a^m@}\) and \({@a@}^{@m+1@} = {@a^(m+1)@}\).</p>
<div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="Graph of y = {#a#} to the power x, and the horizontal line y = {#b2#}. They meet at x approximately {#ta2#}, between {#m#} and {#m+1#}.">
[[jsxgraph width="380px" height="300px"]]
(function() {
  var X0 = -0.5, X1 = {#m+1.6#}, Y1 = {#a^(m+1)*1.05#}, P = [[{#float(ex2)#}, {#b2#}, 'x ≈ {#ta2#}']];
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[X0 - (X1 - X0)*0.12, Y1*1.08, X1, -Y1*0.12], axis:true, grid:false,
      showNavigation:false, showCopyright:false, pan:{enabled:false}, zoom:{enabled:false}});
  b.create('functiongraph', [function(x){ return Math.pow({#a#}, x); }, X0, X1], {strokeColor:'#1f5fa8', strokeWidth:2, highlight:false});
  b.create('line', [[0, {#b2#}], [1, {#b2#}]], {straightFirst:true, straightLast:true, strokeColor:'#2e9d5b', dash:2, highlight:false, fixed:true});
  b.create('segment', [[{#float(ex2)#}, 0], [{#float(ex2)#}, {#b2#}]], {strokeColor:'#c0392b', dash:1, highlight:false, fixed:true});
  for (var i = 0; i < P.length; i++) { var right = P[i][0] > X0 + 0.6*(X1 - X0);   // labels on the right half go to the left of the point
    b.create('point', [P[i][0], P[i][1]], {name:P[i][2], size:3, fixed:true, color:'#c0392b', showInfobox:false,
      label:{offset:[right ? -8 : 8, 10], anchorX:right ? 'right' : 'left', fontSize:12, cssStyle:'background:rgba(255,255,255,0.85)'}}); }
  b.create('text', [X1, -Y1*0.07, 'x'], {anchorX:'right', fontSize:13, fixed:true});
  b.create('text', [X0 - (X1 - X0)*0.1, Y1*1.03, 'y = {#a#}^x'], {fontSize:13, fixed:true});
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
